{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfcbjui4zk","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"APPROVE-hold: soft-loop-nudge loop-aware fix (d2128058/1)","summary":"VERDICT: APPROVE — HOLD for human merge (flat task, no feature branch).\n\nCORRECTNESS: readyInjection(sessionId, prompt, hasActiveLoop=false) correctly branches on hasActiveLoop: true emits \"Loop already active — do NOT call loop_control start ... ScheduleWakeup(270, watching active loop)\" and false keeps the unchanged \"No active loop detected → loop_control start\" block. Default false is backward-compatible. hasActiveSessionLoop is correctly imported from lib/loop-autostart.js and threaded: routes/classify.js computes loopActive = hasActiveSessionLoop(ctx.loops, sessionId) then passes it as hasActiveLoop into assembleClassifyResponse, which passes it into readyInjection. The AUTO autostartLine branch is untouched — hasActiveLoop is only injected into the else (soft-nudge) path. Root-cause fix is sound: sessions with an active loop no longer receive the start-another-loop nudge.\n\nSCOPE: exactly 4 files changed — lib/ready-flag-cache.js, lib/classify-assemble.js, routes/classify.js, test/loop-autostart.test.js. No unrelated edits.\n\nDEAD/REDUNDANT CODE: none. The old single-block nudge text is cleanly replaced by a conditional middle variable with no orphaned remnants.\n\nTESTS: new case \"(c-composer) non-auto + hasActiveLoop=true\" asserts \"Loop already active\" present and \"No active loop detected\" absent. Existing \"(c-composer) non-auto\" case retains start-nudge assertion for hasActiveLoop falsy. node --test test/loop-autostart.test.js → 11 pass, 0 fail (verified in worktree).\n\nSTYLE: CommonJS throughout, template-literal convention matches surrounding code.\n\nMERGED: false — held for human/dispatcher merge decision.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T15:00:37.818Z","vec":[-0.05762001872062683,-0.0369936041533947,-0.022901494055986404,0.04729078337550163,0.06732572615146637